(PREFACE) Tj T*
(TO THE FIRST EDITION.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The following pages were written in compliance with the solicitations of) Tj T*
(many esteemed friends, who were desirous that I should lay before the) Tj T*
(public an outline of my life and travels, and give to the English nation) Tj T*
(a description of the domestic habits and religious opinions of my) Tj T*
(countrymen in Syria.  However incompetent I may have proved for the task,) Tj T*
(I trust that what I have written may not be wholly uninteresting; and) Tj T*
(above all, it is my earnest hope, that my feeble efforts to arouse the) Tj T*
(generous interest of the English for the welfare and improvement of my) Tj T*
(native land, may not prove without use.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In choosing the title which is prefixed to my humble work, I have acted) Tj T*
(upon the long-established usage of my countrymen of speaking) Tj T*
(parabolically, a practice which has existed from the days of Job down to) Tj T*
(the present time.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I cannot conclude without offering my heartfelt thanks to my friend, the) Tj T*
(Rev. Wm. Frederick Witts, Fellow of King?s College, Cambridge, for the) Tj T*
(valuable assistance he has rendered me in revising these pages for the) Tj T*
ET
endstream
