(press.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                                                                     R. A.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(18, _Cambridge-square_, _Hyde Park_,) Tj T*
(            _May_, 1853.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                                 PREFACE) Tj T*
(                          TO THE SECOND EDITION.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(One thousand copies, which constituted the First Edition of this work,) Tj T*
(having been disposed of within six months, I cannot allow another to go) Tj T*
(forth without expressing the satisfaction I feel at the liberal) Tj T*
(encouragement it has met with, and the gratitude I entertain towards my) Tj T*
(English readers for their indulgence towards it.  My acknowledgments are) Tj T*
(also due to the Press, for the very favourable notices with which it has) Tj T*
(been invariably honoured by them.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The same hope which animated my labours, and induced me to present them) Tj T*
(to the public, still cheers me on, namely, that of engaging the attention) Tj T*
(and exciting the interest of the English nation in the fate and prospects) Tj T*
(of Syria, my beloved country: a land dear to every thinking mind from its) Tj T*
(sacred associations, and richly meriting the attention of the man of) Tj T*
(business and the traveller, from its undeveloped material resources, and) Tj T*
(from its picturesque beauty and healthy climate.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I can only allude to, in order to deplore, the state of war which now) Tj T*
(agitates and exhausts it; but in whatever manner the dispute may be) Tj T*
(settled, I have confidence that England and France will see justice done) Tj T*
(to an outraged country; and also, that the patriotic cause of our) Tj T*
(government will finally triumph over its enemies; for, under the generous) Tj T*
(and tolerant sway of Abdul Medjid Khan, and his enlightened ministers,) Tj T*
(far more is to be effected for the welfare of every class of his) Tj T*
(subjects, than are likely to arise from the interference of any foreign) Tj T*
(power; and I am sure that the more intelligent portion of the Orthodox) Tj T*
(Greek population are fully aware of this, and that they are, as they) Tj T*
(ought to be, loyally disposed towards the Sultan, their sovereign.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As I am now on the eve of quitting England for the East, I take this) Tj T*
(opportunity of publicly giving expression to my heartfelt sense of the) Tj T*
(uniform kindness and courtesy I have met with from all ranks in this) Tj T*
(mighty empire; also, of once more expressing the earnest hope, that when) Tj T*
(this present contest shall have ceased, British energy, philanthropy, and) Tj T*
(capital, may be induced to promote the commercial and educational) Tj T*
(development of the population and resources of my native land.  She) Tj T*
(possesses many natural treasures?she is eager for improvement?she is not) Tj T*
(far distant.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(If to this end the following pages shall have, even in the smallest) Tj T*
(degree contributed, I shall enjoy the high gratification of believing) Tj T*
(that neither my life nor my labour has been in vain.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
