(Months rolled on.  Merchants were at that period carrying on a) Tj T*
(comparatively thriving trade at Beyrout.  The novelty of the scene that) Tj T*
(presented itself on my first arrival there had gradually worn off.  In my) Tj T*
(leisure hours I rambled along the sandy beach, gathering shells, and) Tj T*
(wading ankle deep into the surf, at first with ill-suppressed fear and) Tj T*
(trembling; but the example of other boys emboldening me to venture into) Tj T*
(the water, I finished by becoming quite an adept in the art of swimming.) Tj T*
(Then the ships were a source of wonder and surprise, as they sailed in) Tj T*
(and out of the harbour, like gigantic swans floating over the waves.) Tj T*
(These also had ceased to excite interest, for I had been on board,) Tj T*
(handled the tarry ropes, walked the deck, and suffered inconvenience from) Tj T*
(the disagreeable motion, so that these also had ceased to be a marvel.) Tj T*
(Thus time rolled on, and I had well nigh forgotten all my regrets at) Tj T*
(leaving Lebanon and the hospitable abode of my uncle, when the unexpected) Tj T*
(event alluded to in the foregoing chapter, transpired.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
