(this knowledge having led to preferment and subsequent opulence, my) Tj T*
(friends conceived the idea of placing me under the care of some of the) Tj T*
(excellent American Missionaries, for tuition in English and other) Tj T*
(European languages.  It was not without reluctance that I obeyed the) Tj T*
(mandate of my friends, but as implicit obedience to their will was a) Tj T*
(primary consideration, bidding adieu to my many kind acquaintances, I) Tj T*
(retraced my steps, and in the course of a few days was once again in the) Tj T*
(bosom of my own dear family.  The Americans have always numbered amongst) Tj T*
(their fraternity a medical officer; and it was mainly attributable to) Tj T*
(this fact, that myself, as well as many other Syrian lads, were happily) Tj T*
(blessed with the opportunity of receiving a good moral education.  I was) Tj T*
(just entering on my sixteenth year when I first joined the American) Tj T*
(school; still too young to have any deeply rooted prejudices or ideas,) Tj T*
(though luckily old enough to appreciate the value of the opportunity thus) Tj T*
