(never so much enjoyed a journey as in his pleasant and instructive) Tj T*
(company.  Our plan of route was to first visit Cyprus and Asia Minor,) Tj T*
(then the northern towns and villages of Syria, and so travel southwards) Tj T*
(as far as the limits of Syria and Palestine.  All things being prepared,) Tj T*
(we set sail from Beyrout late one evening in a small felucca, which,) Tj T*
(nevertheless, in fine weather, sailed remarkably well; and, upon the) Tj T*
(whole, we were pretty comfortable on board, the entire use of the boat,) Tj T*
(to the exclusion of other passengers, having been contracted for.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
