(face; or to have his name bandied about to the world in some gaudily) Tj T*
(bound book of travels, in which authors have seen fit to make sport of) Tj T*
(men, who, in all probability, sacrificed a night?s rest and comfort to) Tj T*
(contribute both towards them in a strange land.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(While on this subject, I may record one instance which came to my) Tj T*
(knowledge, and which was really too scandalous not to be made known.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A party of travellers, for I cannot style them gentlemen, five or six in) Tj T*
(number, were travelling through Syria and Palestine, accompanied by a) Tj T*
