(protect them from punishment if they once gave offence to Europeans.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(After remaining some time at Tripoli, we proceeded to visit the famous) Tj T*
(cedars of Lebanon.  There are at present eleven of these celebrated) Tj T*
(trees, seven of which are supposed to have existed from the time of the) Tj T*
(building of Solomon?s temple.  I need scarcely inform my readers how) Tj T*
(conspicuously these trees have figured in Scriptural metaphors.  The) Tj T*
(prophet Ezekiel speaks in glowing terms of their beauty.  Again, Isaiah) Tj T*
(seems in a remarkable manner to predict their extinction, ?The rest of) Tj T*
(the trees of this forest shall be few that a child may write them.?  How) Tj T*
(literally has this prophecy been fulfilled!) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(On my last visit to Syria I found the priest, to whom the charge of these) Tj T*
(trees is committed, had planted a number of seedlings, though with what) Tj T*
(success I have not yet heard.  A church has also been built on the spot.) Tj T*
(The Arabs believe they were planted by the hands of the Almighty himself,) Tj T*
(and there are innumerable traditions connected with these trees, which I) Tj T*
(hope to give an account of in a future work.  One of these cedars is of) Tj T*
(so great a diameter, that a monk actually hollowed it out and formed a) Tj T*
(sort of room in which he took up his abode.  The trunks are covered with) Tj T*
(names of travellers, many of a very old date cut out with the knife.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
