(captivated by the beauty of the Moslem ladies.  On first arriving, this) Tj T*
(gentleman was well received by the grey-bearded authorities; but he soon) Tj T*
(lost caste; reports and complaints were of every-day occurrence; this) Tj T*
(white stranger would persist in making love to the Moslem ladies, and the) Tj T*
(Moslem girls would persist in making love to him.  This was a dreadful) Tj T*
(state of affairs; but this was not all, for even the old Armenian) Tj T*
(patriarch was roused into wrath by discovering that a timid little) Tj T*
(Armenian girl was actually head over ears in love with the) Tj T*
(feather-crowned stranger, or rather with his money.  There was no) Tj T*
(standing this.  The people said it was a crying shame, and reported it to) Tj T*
(the Cadi, who complained to Nedjid Pasha; and the Pasha, who was one of) Tj T*
(the old school, and a right down Frank hater, complained to the) Tj T*
(Commander-in-Chief of the forces at Beyrout.  The Commander-in-Chief sent) Tj T*
(several officers up to Damascus to investigate the case, which was tried) Tj T*
(in open divan before the Pasha, who summoned such as had charges against) Tj T*
(the gallant officer to appear before him.  The charges brought against) Tj T*
(him were twofold.  First, that he had endeavoured to subvert the minds of) Tj T*
(the people from rendering due homage to Ottoman authority, by asking them) Tj T*
(such significant questions as, for instance, If the English or the French) Tj T*
(were to lay siege to the country, with which of the powers would you) Tj T*
(side?  The second charge was, the heinous offence of making love to some) Tj T*
(score of Turkish damsels, besides the Armenian lady in question.  The) Tj T*
(first charge was thrown out as frivolous, absurd, and annoying; the) Tj T*
(second was fully proved.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
