(    dissatisfaction, he was determined at any cost to get the cleverest) Tj T*
(    man in the kingdom to perform the duties of that office; but he) Tj T*
(    resorted to a curious trial of their talent.  A proclamation was) Tj T*
(    issued, that the sultan offered the highest dignity in the empire to) Tj T*
(    him amongst his subjects, who should be able satisfactorily to) Tj T*
(    perform what he should require; on the other hand, the penalty in) Tj T*
(    case of failure being, that the man so failing should forfeit his) Tj T*
(    head.  Under such circumstances, the aspirants were not over) Tj T*
(    numerous, but still there were not wanting ambitious men, who were) Tj T*
(    willing to place their heads in danger for the attainment of a) Tj T*
(    position, which perhaps they least of any of the people of the) Tj T*
(    country were fitted for.  At last, a presumptuous tailor offered) Tj T*
(    himself as a candidate, and was in due course ushered into the) Tj T*
(    presence of royalty.  The poor maker of garments found the sultan) Tj T*
(    reclining on a carpet; and, hanging on a nail in the wall of the) Tj T*
(    room, was a solitary counterpane; and in this counterpane the) Tj T*
(    solution of the whole of the difficulty lay?the task being to cover) Tj T*
(    the sultan entirely over with it.  When the tailor first tried, to) Tj T*
(    his consternation he found it too short by two good spans.  He then) Tj T*
(    suggested that another should be introduced; but the sultan laughed) Tj T*
(    and hooted at the idea.  At last a bright notion flashed across the) Tj T*
(    tailor.  He had long been accustomed to the nefarious art of) Tj T*
(    cabbaging, so he set his inventive faculties to work, to find out how) Tj T*
(    he could best cabbage a piece from the length of the sultan?s body,) Tj T*
(    or, in other words, reduce it into as small a compass as could) Tj T*
(    possibly be effected.  Bethinking himself luckily of a little cane he) Tj T*
(    usually carried in his girdle, he first covered the sultan?s head,) Tj T*
(    his feet remaining uncovered; he removed the embroidered slippers,) Tj T*
(    and stealthily bringing out his cane, caught the sultan a severe blow) Tj T*
(    across the soles of his feet, that he involuntarily tucked them up,) Tj T*
(    thus drawing himself into a sufficiently small compass, and the) Tj T*
(    tailor, availing himself of this circumstance, instantly tucked the) Tj T*
(    counterpane round him, and thus effectually succeeded in entirely) Tj T*
(    covering him, at the same time telling him he must always take care) Tj T*
(    to stretch his legs according to his covering.?) Tj T*
