(That which, in my opinion, establishes the resources and vitality of the) Tj T*
(Turkish empire is, that if one of the serious struggles to which it has) Tj T*
(been exposed for the last forty years, were to have happened to any other) Tj T*
(power, it would either have crippled it or caused its entire destruction.) Tj T*
(Turkey, on the contrary, has, during this space of time, experienced the) Tj T*
(severest trials, as, for instance, the Greek revolution, the destruction) Tj T*
(of the Janissaries in 1826 \(who at that time constituted her army\), the) Tj T*
(annihilation of her fleet at Navarino, the protracted war with Russia,) Tj T*
(the civil war with Egypt, and the many partial outbreaks caused by the) Tj T*
(machinations of European powers; in spite of all these, so far from) Tj T*
(sinking, Turkey, at this time possesses, besides irregular troops and) Tj T*
(auxiliaries, a regular and well-disciplined army and a splendid fleet,) Tj T*
(and is endeavouring still further to increase, and re-establish peace,) Tj T*
(and internal security; and also to find the best means of enriching her) Tj T*
(treasury without burdening her subjects; and I trust, that, under the) Tj T*
(beneficial government of the present benign Sultan, and his enlightened) Tj T*
(ministers \(in spite of the fanatical party\), Turkey will yet make great) Tj T*
(progress in civilisation and all its concomitant blessings.  At least, if) Tj T*
(she does not, it will not be for want of exertion on the part of Abdul) Tj T*
(Medjid to introduce into his empire a thorough reform, himself setting an) Tj T*
(example to his subjects of forbearance and goodly feeling towards the) Tj T*
(many sects dwelling within the boundaries of his empire.  The truth of) Tj T*
(these views has been amply proved by the gallant resistance offered by) Tj T*
(Turkey at the present crisis to the unjust aggressions of Russia.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Just before leaving Constantinople, a circumstance occurred which created) Tj T*
(quite a sensation amongst all classes and creeds.  An Armenian girl, the) Tj T*
(daughter of very respectable parents, formed a secret attachment to a) Tj T*
(young Moslem, in the service of the Sultan.  The lovers managed to) Tj T*
(contrive interviews without exciting the suspicion of the girl?s friends;) Tj T*
(and eventually the girl fled to her lover, embraced the Mahommedan faith,) Tj T*
(and was regularly married to him.  Sometime after they had been married,) Tj T*
(the young girl went to call upon her mother, most probably without her) Tj T*
(husband?s consent.  The mother and all her relations bemoaning with many) Tj T*
(tears her apostasy, implored of the girl not to return to her husband,) Tj T*
(but to be received once again into her mother church.  The girl, overcome) Tj T*
(by emotion for the moment, yielded a ready consent; and for her better) Tj T*
(security, it was agreed that she should be placed within the Armenian) Tj T*
(asylum.  This was accordingly done, and the husband made vain search for) Tj T*
(his missing bride.  Meanwhile the young lady got tired of her) Tj T*
(confinement, and very possibly of the treatment she received from the) Tj T*
(over-zealous attendants at the asylum, and accordingly contrived, through) Tj T*
(the window of the room where she was confined, to convey a message to her) Tj T*
(husband.  The husband immediately complained to the authorities; who) Tj T*
(without delay demanded the girl of the bishop.  The prelate at first) Tj T*
(denied any knowledge of the person in question.  A military force was) Tj T*
(then sent to bring her away at any hazard; and a parley commenced between) Tj T*
(the commandant and the bishop, in which the latter gave his _parole) Tj T*
(d?honneur_, that if the troops were withdrawn he would conduct the girl) Tj T*
(himself next day before the divan, and she should there declare publicly,) Tj T*
(which of the two faiths she of her own free will would wish to embrace.) Tj T*
