(first-class ticket direct from Marseilles to Paris by diligence.  On my) Tj T*
(arrival at Lyons, I was told that I must remain until next morning,) Tj T*
(unless I consented to travel in an inferior part of the carriage.  This,) Tj T*
(notwithstanding my urgent remonstrances, I was compelled to do, owing to) Tj T*
(the necessity of my being in Paris by a certain date; and, though exposed) Tj T*
(to many inconveniences, I was so fortunate as to arrive there in time.) Tj T*
(My stay at Paris was limited to a few days, and I then came on to London) Tj T*
(and delivered my despatches to his excellency our respected ambassador,) Tj T*
(who immediately recognised me as one of his suite, and who has ever since) Tj T*
(continued to treat me with the greatest urbanity.  So soon as my official) Tj T*
(duties permitted, I went the round of my kind friends in London, and) Tj T*
(amongst others, was delighted to see the Honourable George Massey, my old) Tj T*
(and well-tried friend, who insisted upon my taking up my abode at his) Tj T*
(house, where I remain surrounded by every comfort and luxury that) Tj T*
(kindness and forethought can provide, and happy in the enjoyment of the) Tj T*
(society of a genuine English family.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The handsome present of horses lately sent by Abbas Pasha to the Queen of) Tj T*
(England, clearly testifies the good feeling existing between the two) Tj T*
(governments, and how much the viceroy wishes to keep up those friendly) Tj T*
(feelings so successfully cultivated and maintained.  One of the horses) Tj T*
(above alluded to is of the largest and most valuable and rare breed; and) Tj T*
(there is little doubt but that the English nation will hereafter be) Tj T*
(indebted to Abbas Pasha for the possession of a breed of horses now) Tj T*
(unknown in England.  The horses were sent to this country under the) Tj T*
(charge of Nubar Bey, an Armenian, a native of Smyrna, a relative of) Tj T*
(Boghas Bey, who is much esteemed by the Pasha and the Egyptians.  He) Tj T*
(received a first-rate education in Europe, and speaks several of its) Tj T*
(languages with fluency; he accompanied Ibrahim Pasha on his visit to this) Tj T*
