(?You asked me, before leaving Stamboul, to convey to you as well as I) Tj T*
(could by letter my first impressions of England and the English.  Your) Tj T*
(Excellency can hardly conceive the difficulty of the task which you have) Tj T*
(allotted me.  However arduous the undertaking may be, I shall endeavour,) Tj T*
(to the best of my poor abilities, to satisfy your curiosity, and fulfil) Tj T*
(my rash promise.  In our own dear village, and indeed in the most active) Tj T*
(and bustling towns of Syria, the silence and monotony of the houses are) Tj T*
(only occasionally broken in upon by the busy hum of human voices?the) Tj T*
(clattering hoofs of horses and mules?the braying of donkeys, and the) Tj T*
(merry tinkling bell of the caravan.  The sweet song of the bulbul and) Tj T*
(other summer birds, with the buzzing of the honey-bee, are the familiar) Tj T*
(sounds to which we are from our infancy accustomed.  Stately forest) Tj T*
(trees?mountains and hills?valleys and dales?citron groves and) Tj T*
(orchards?the bright plumage of birds and the painted wings of butterflies) Tj T*
(are the every-day pictures, furnished by the hand of nature, and on which) Tj T*
(alone our eyes have been content to dwell.  The sound of chariot wheels) Tj T*
(has through centuries been hushed and sunk into oblivion, together with) Tj T*
(the fiery-spirited warriors that guided them.  Such is the quiet state of) Tj T*
(affairs in our own loved country of Syria.  Now, therefore, imagine) Tj T*
(yourself blindfolded and transported as though by magic into the very) Tj T*
(centre of the city of London.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?Previously, however, a vast extent of ocean has to be traversed, which) Tj T*
(is accomplished in an incredibly short space of time, during which period) Tj T*
(much suffering from sea-sickness is to be expected, and many are) Tj T*
(compelled to keep to their cabins, creeping only upon deck occasionally) Tj T*
(to cheer the heart with a distant glimpse of land, as Malta and Gibraltar) Tj T*
(have appeared to view, and as speedily vanished from sight, leaving, like) Tj T*
(the false mirage, no trace behind.  At last the shores of _Ingleterra_) Tj T*
(are discerned.  The announcement is heard with indescribable delight, for) Tj T*
(the term of purgatory is about to expire.  Well wrapped in a _burnoos_,) Tj T*
(for, although midsummer, the air is keen, you scramble upon deck, and) Tj T*
(being comfortably seated, take a first survey of the famed shores of) Tj T*
(Britain.  As far as the eye can stretch, the whole land appears to be) Tj T*
(what is really the case, in a high state of cultivation.  Houses and) Tj T*
(windmills innumerable meet the view, and a vast number of smoking) Tj T*
(minarets, which on inquiry prove to be the chimneys of countless) Tj T*
(factories.  But you are not left long to consider these matters?what is) Tj T*
(occurring in the more immediate vicinity of the steamer rivets your) Tj T*
(attention.  Thousands of vessels of all sizes, shapes, and nations, are) Tj T*
(moving up and down the channel.  Gigantic men-of-war steamers?still) Tj T*
(larger mail-packets, ships-of-the-line, frigates, sloops, gun-brigs,) Tj T*
