({210}  EUPHRATES AND THE EAST.?On Saturday last, a lecture announced) Tj T*
(under the above title, was delivered at the Assembly Rooms in this city,) Tj T*
(by Dr. J. B. Thompson, a gentleman who has just returned from a medical) Tj T*
(mission in Turkey.  Capt. Saumarez, R.N., presided, and a very numerous) Tj T*
(audience of ladies and gentlemen attended on the occasion.  The lecture) Tj T*
(was so desultory in its course, that it will not admit of analysis;) Tj T*
(nevertheless, it was exceedingly interesting, and formed an important) Tj T*
(addition to our information respecting a country which is the cradle of) Tj T*
(the world.  Dr. Thompson, it appears, was sent to Asiatic Turkey on a) Tj T*
(medical mission by an association of English gentlemen, amongst whom was) Tj T*
(the Earl of Ellesmere; and having opened a free hospital at Damascus, and) Tj T*
(acquired the Arabic language, he enjoyed rare facilities for obtaining a) Tj T*
(knowledge of the manners, feelings, and circumstances of the population.) Tj T*
(There is not only more toleration for Christians in Turkey, but less) Tj T*
