(corruption and injustice than under the powers which seek to dismember) Tj T*
(it.  He described the Turkish rulers as sensible men, ever ready to carry) Tj T*
(on any improvements suggested to them.  The missionaries would effect far) Tj T*
(more if, instead of teaching doctrines to adults, they educated the) Tj T*
(females prior to their seclusion in the harems.  There was no impediment) Tj T*
(to the establishment of female schools; and, therefore, if these) Tj T*
(secondary means were adopted, the condition of the young might be raised,) Tj T*
(the prejudices of the parents might be abated, and a foundation might be) Tj T*
(laid for the civilization of the East.  The principal feature of the) Tj T*
(lecture, however, was the description of a new route to India.  Instead) Tj T*
(of passengers proceeding by Alexandria, Cairo, across the sandy Egyptian) Tj T*
(Desert, and through the Red Sea, it was suggested that they should land) Tj T*
(at the mouth of the river Orontes, near Antioch, in Syria, and pass) Tj T*
(through a rich and beautiful country to Belis.  There, embarking on the) Tj T*
(river Euphrates, they would descend through the land of Paradise to) Tj T*
(Bussora on the Persian Gulf and from thence proceed straight to Bombay or) Tj T*
(Calcutta.  The advantages of this new route were healthiness and) Tj T*
(rapidity.  The journey to India by Suez occupied twenty-eight days, and) Tj T*
(entailed much suffering in crossing the Desert, and in traversing the) Tj T*
(unhealthy Red Sea.  The transit from Antioch to Belis would occupy two) Tj T*
(days by railway through a country so rich and fertile that it would) Tj T*
(become peopled if communication were opened up.  The entire journey to) Tj T*
(India would be shortened seven days, the route being not only better but) Tj T*
(shorter by at least 300 miles.  The saving of time would be still greater) Tj T*
(if a railway were formed along the bank of the Euphrates from Belis to) Tj T*
(Bussora.  Dr. Thompson addressed himself to the objections which had been) Tj T*
(made to the route by the Euphrates.  It had been said, that Col.) Tj T*
(Chesney?s exploring expedition failed; but this was incorrect.  Col.) Tj T*
(Chesney?s difficulties arose partly from his having fixed upon Barick,) Tj T*
(higher up than Belis, as his terminus, and partly from the want of native) Tj T*
(pilots.  The river is subject to squalls, the signs of which are familiar) Tj T*
(to those who live on its banks; but Col. Chesney employed none of the) Tj T*
(navigators, and one of his steamers having been upset, the river in) Tj T*
(consequence got a bad name.  It had been said, too, that the Bedouin) Tj T*
(Arabs are ill-disposed towards the navigation of the Euphrates.  This Dr.) Tj T*
(Thompson denied on his own knowledge, having visited all the chiefs along) Tj T*
(the banks, and he declared, contrary to the general opinion, that the) Tj T*
(Bedouins are a benevolent, generous, noble-hearted race.  It might be) Tj T*
(true, he observed, that during the progress of Col. Chesney?s expedition,) Tj T*
(the Bedouins were prejudiced against the navigation of the river; but the) Tj T*
(fact was, there were powers which thought they had an interest in) Tj T*
(misrepresenting the intentions of the English in the East.  This feeling) Tj T*
(had, however, been dissipated by more correct knowledge.  Dr. Thompson) Tj T*
(added, that he had submitted the plan of the Euphrates route to the) Tj T*
(Turkish Sultan, who immediately perceived its advantages over the old) Tj T*
(route through Egypt, and would strongly support it.  One feature of the) Tj T*
(plan, he also stated, would be the establishment of a school for children) Tj T*
(at Antioch, the climate of which is delightful; and while officers in) Tj T*
(India might come there on furlough, without losing certain advantages, as) Tj T*
(they would still be within the confines of Asia, their friends in Europe) Tj T*
(would find it an easy and delightful trip to visit them at that place.) Tj T*
(Dr. Thompson pointed out other and more general advantages, which would) Tj T*
